          %h1#hsets h-Sets
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#equivalent_characterizations"} Equivalent characterizations
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#hedbergs_theorem"} Hedberg’s theorem
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelationToInternalSets"} Relation to internal sets
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#PretoposOfHsets"} Pretopos of hsets
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            an
            %em h-set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            – hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            – with the special property that any two of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terms"} terms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y : X
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"}> equivalent
            ) in an at most essentially unique way, hence that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x = y) : Type
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
          %p
            The notion of h-set is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
            object into homotopy type theory, essentially an internalization of the notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            (or possibly of
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preset"} preset
            %em
              %a{:href => "#RelationToInternalSets"} Relation to internal sets
            for more on this.
          %p
            h-Sets can also be regarded as a way of embedding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional type theory
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sums"} dependent sums
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+products"} dependent products
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isSet(A)
            as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                  %mi isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isSet(A) \coloneqq \prod_{x\colon A} \prod_{y\colon A} isProp(\mathrm{Id}_{A}(x, y))
          %p
            (using any equivalent definition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate"} predicate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isProp"} isProp
            for
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-propositions"} h-propositions
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            types and “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Id}_A
            ” denotes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            In other words, the only relationship between two elements of an h-set is whether they are equal; there is no room for more than one path between them. By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/beta+reduction"} beta-reducing
            this definition, we can express it as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isSet(A) \coloneqq \prod_{x,y\colon A} \prod_{p,q\colon \mathrm{Id}_A(x, y)} \mathrm{Id}_{\mathrm{Id}_A(x, y)}(p, q)
          %p
            In other words, any two parallel paths in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are equal.
          %p
            A provably
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+homotopy+type+theory"} equivalent
            definition is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isSet(A) \coloneqq \prod_{x\colon A} \prod_{p\colon \mathrm{Id}_A(x, x)} \mathrm{Id}_{\mathrm{Id}_A(x, x)}(p, \mathrm{refl}_A(x))
          %p
            This says that a version of Streicher’s “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+K"}> axiom K
            ” holds for h-sets. (See also at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+UIP"} axiom UIP
          %p
            Another definition of a h-set is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+type"} local type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} const
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{const}_{A, S^1}:A \to (S^1 \to A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functions"} constant functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \to A
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+type"} circle type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} const
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo :
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} const
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} const
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isSet}(A) \coloneqq \prod_{f:S^1 \to A} \sum_{y:\sum_{x:A} \mathrm{Id}_{S^1 \to A}(\mathrm{const}_{A, S^1}(x), f)} \prod_{z:\sum_{x:A} \mathrm{Id}_{S^1 \to A}(\mathrm{const}_{A, S^1}(x), f)} \mathrm{Id}_{\sum_{x:A} \mathrm{Id}_{S^1 \to A}(\mathrm{const}_{A, S^1}(x), f)}(y, z)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Most (non-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"}> higher
                )
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
                are h-sets (assuming that all their parameters and indices are so). In particular, the type of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
                is an h-set. This can be proven from Theorem
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DecidableIsSet"}
                below.
            %li
              %p
                In a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set-level+type+theory"} set-level type theory
                %em all
                types are h-sets.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
                is the only well-known property that implies that
                %em not
                all types are h-sets. In particular, it implies that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+type"} universe type
                is not an h-set, and that many
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+types"} higher inductive types
                are not h-sets.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#equivalent_characterizations Equivalent characterizations
          %p
            There are some equivalent characterizations of a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            being an h-set:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is an h-set if and only if all its identity types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=_A y
                have
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+support"} split support
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo :
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{(x,y:A)} \Vert x=y\Vert \to (x=y)
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#KECA"} (KECA)
            %li
              %p
                More generally,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is an h-set if and only if there is some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi Prop
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:A\to A\to Prop
                which is reflexive (i.e.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo :
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{(x:A)} R(x,x)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo :
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{(x,y:A)} R(x,y) \to (x=y)
                = succeed "." do
